Fire Emblem is back and this year it's  leaving the classrooms of three houses  behind here is everything you need to  know about Fire Emblem engage  [Music]  in Fire Emblem engage 1 000 years have  passed since the four kingdoms  cooperated with each other and with  heroes from other worlds to seal away  the fell dragon on the continent of  Elios as the evil prepares to reawaken  you emerge as a leader the Divine Dragon  a chosen hero who can bring back the  heroes from other Realms and seal the  chaos Dragon once again like other Fire  Emblem protagonists alir can be female  or male with a similar red and blue  hairstyle in both instances  [Music]  like other Fire Emblem games engage will  be a turn-based tactical combat game  with a wide array of original characters  that you can upgrade and customize to  your liking your time is split between  the Tactical tile based combat and a hub  area where you can interact with other  characters this non-combat section is a  floating Fortress called the somniel but  hope that thought we'll come right back  to the somnia soon first let's dive into  combat fans of traditional Fire Emblem  games Rejoice engage is bringing back  the weapon triangle a rock paper scissor  mechanic of weapon advantages that was  altered in Fire Emblem 3 houses swords B  axes axes beat Spears and Spears beat  sword taking advantage of the weapons  triangle inflix break which prevents the  defending unit from countering in that  Skirmish weapons outside of the triangle  such as bows daggers and spell tomes are  weak to physical attacks Fire Emblem age  also does away with weapon durability  once you find or purchase a weapon it's  yours to keep this change could mean  less time managing a unit's inventory  and more time battling enemies and  chatting up comrades Fire Emblem is  class based so different classes will  specialize in certain weapon types and  as you upgrade your classes you'll gain  new specializations at the center of  engages combat is the engage mechanic as  you progress through the story you  unlock emblem rings that can be equipped  on any party member each emblem ring  houses the spirit of a character from a  previous Fire Emblem game and when given  to a party member they combine for  improved stats and some powerful  abilities you can mix emblem rings with  any character in your party for varying  effects and strategies some combinations  can lead to incredibly mobile party  members While others could significantly  buff a character's strength stat some  combinations may work better than others  but every party member can force bonds  with every classic character housed in  an emblem ring every Mainline Fire  Emblem game is represented via the  emblem Rings like bonds formed between  units bonds between party members and  emblem Rings increase the effectiveness  of that pair each ring has an upgrade  path for each character in your crew  these upgrade paths can give a character  permanent stat boosts and new skills  that are unique to a specific emblem  ring there are also a handful of tweaks  to moment-to-moment combat as well most  notably now you have direct control over  a character's movement rather than  selecting a unit and plotting a path for  them you can freely move around the  battle before committing to a tile and  attacking it's not a huge change but it  does give a little more flexibility and  precision to your movements and now  let's talk about the non-combat portions  of the game inside the somnil you'll  have access to areas like the plaza  which contains the Armory and the item  shop the ring chamber is home to all of  the emblem Rings you've collected this  is where you can inherit skills from  emblems create and meld Bond rings for  stat boosts and polish your battle  tarnished rings for an even deeper Bond  the arena is the perfect place to  practice your combat skills while still  earning experience and some other  benefits in a familiar vein the Tower of  Trials is a location on the far end of  the somnil that lets you take on a  series of battles in order to earn  in-game rewards but this Hub area isn't  all about buying weapons and practicing  battle scenarios the somnil is also  where you'll get to know your allies  better in Fire Emblem you're not just  chatting with buddies for the hell of it  the game also tends to give bonuses for  units battling side by side if they've  developed special Bonds in the  non-combat portions since food is  perfect at bringing people together you  can share a meal with a friend at the  cafe Terrace not hungry give your allies  a gift instead to deepen your bond other  activities in the somnia include fishing  fortune telling wyvern riding managing a  farm yard buying clothes at the boutique  and partaking in some strength training  for temporary stat Buffs  [Music]  Fire Emblem engage is set to release on  January 20th 2023 exclusively for the  Nintendo switch pre-orders are available  right now and there are two editions of  the game standard and divine the  standard edition digital and physical  comes with the base game and nothing  more the Divine Edition comes with the  base game as well as a steelbook case  our cards an art book and a pretty cool  poster but beware the Divine Edition  sold out quickly so it may be harder to  find there will be four paid DLCs that  will launch throughout 2023 with the  first wave of the expansion becoming  available the same day as the base game  on January 20th this first wave includes  additional support items new accessories  a silver card and additional emblems  like the emblem bracelet for edogard  Dimitri and Claude all in one and  another for Tiki Fire Emblem engage  brings back a lot of familiar faces and  a core mechanic is being able to summon  Fire Emblem Heroes to the battlefield  players can probably expect the other  waves of DLC to also include pass Fire  Emblem characters from different titles  that's everything you need to know about  Fire Emblem and Gage the classrooms are  gone and the weapons triangle is back  there are more than enough old faces to  tug at your Nostalgia for the series and  plenty of activities to get lost in  outside of battle drop a comment below  letting us know your favorite Fire  Emblem game thus far for more videos on  engage including our review keep it  locked to GameSpot  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

